    {
      "id": "c6c31b5340f45947ad5bebe5c9153ac2cd75a55e",
      "short_id": "c6c31b53",
      "created_at": "2023-01-06T14:11:32.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "6902eebfb6c00af53c9039103d75c3b74565ec2f"
      ],
      "title": "PFCP: organise list of IEs differently and refactor common decode-function",
      "message": "PFCP: organise list of IEs differently and refactor common decode-function\n\nAdding new enterpries IES was a bit cumbersome because the text and\ndecode functions would need to be added to separate lists. This was\nalready a source for consistency bugs, as one inconsistency was already\nfound in the Travelping list.\n\nThe new organisation of the enterprise IES keeps this information\ntogether and makes adding new ones easier.\n\nAnother advantage of the new system is the ability of having gaps in the\nIE-type-space. Instead of using a contigous array, a sorted table\ncontaining the ie-type is now used. Lookup now happens using\nbinary-search instead of array-indexing.\n\nTogether with the changes requried to use the new datastructure, the\ncommon decoder-function has been reworked.\n\nA last cleanup in this commit is the registering of the per-IE\nsubtree-arrays. This code was hard to read and hase been improved upon.\n",
      "author_name": "jpeeraer",
      "author_email": "joris.peeraer@nokia.com",
      "authored_date": "2023-01-05T14:57:09.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Alexis La Goutte",
      "committer_email": "alexis.lagoutte@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2023-01-06T14:11:32.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/c6c31b5340f45947ad5bebe5c9153ac2cd75a55e"
    },
    {
      "id": "6902eebfb6c00af53c9039103d75c3b74565ec2f",
      "short_id": "6902eebf",
      "created_at": "2023-01-06T14:11:32.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "0fc010a36cad8ae104f80a719917924b5f1e9494"
      ],
      "title": "PFCP: make dissectors return dissected length",
      "message": "PFCP: make dissectors return dissected length\n\nMaking each IE-dissector return how much data was actually decoded, allows\na central check to be done to check all data was decoded and no data\nremains undecoded.\n\nPreviously this check was spread around more than a 100 times around in\nthe code. This cleans up a lot of duplicated code-blocks and reduces the\nplaces where the wrong type of expert-info can be generated (as not each\nversion of this code-block will have been tested).\n",
      "author_name": "jpeeraer",
      "author_email": "joris.peeraer@nokia.com",
      "authored_date": "2023-01-05T13:09:08.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Alexis La Goutte",
      "committer_email": "alexis.lagoutte@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2023-01-06T14:11:32.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/6902eebfb6c00af53c9039103d75c3b74565ec2f"
    },
    {
      "id": "0fc010a36cad8ae104f80a719917924b5f1e9494",
      "short_id": "0fc010a3",
      "created_at": "2023-01-06T14:11:32.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "14c68dfc856801191fb4a87c8b788e7880140ca9"
      ],
      "title": "PFCP: remove ie-decoder functions that are empty wrapper around dissect_pfcp_grouped_ie",
      "message": "PFCP: remove ie-decoder functions that are empty wrapper around dissect_pfcp_grouped_ie\n\nBy simplifying the dissect_pfcp_grouped_ie calls, some dissector\nfunctions have become a simple wrapper to dissect_pfcp_grouped_ie\nwith even the same arguments.\n\nThese functions are removed and the dissect_pfcp_grouped_ie function is\nused directly where references to these old functions were used\nprevisouly.\n",
      "author_name": "jpeeraer",
      "author_email": "joris.peeraer@nokia.com",
      "authored_date": "2023-01-05T11:16:58.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Alexis La Goutte",
      "committer_email": "alexis.lagoutte@gmail.com",
